From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dnsapi: record type names, question writer, context handles, cache table

- DnsRecordStringForType, DnsRecordStringForWritableType and
  DnsRecordTypeForName were unexported stubs. They now translate between
  record types and their names (case-insensitive, honouring the length),
  and the writable variant refuses the query-only and transaction types.
- DnsWriteQuestionToBuffer_UTF8/_W build a real query: header in host
  order (Xid, recursion desired, one question), the name in wire format
  and the type and class IN. A buffer that is too small gives
  ERROR_MORE_DATA and the needed size; bad labels give ERROR_INVALID_NAME.
- DnsAcquireContextHandle_* return a real handle that
  DnsReleaseContextHandle frees; the flush calls no longer log FIXMEs.
- DnsGetCacheDataTable lists the hosts file as A and AAAA entries (and
  localhost, which resolves without one), one per
  name, each separately allocated so DnsFree works.
